# Early Stage Compatibility

This project is still in its initial development phase and has never been released.

- Do not add compatibility layers, migrations, fallback readers, or shims for formats or APIs that only existed on the current unreleased branch.
- When a storage format, API contract, command shape, or frontend state model is wrong, replace it directly instead of preserving the old behavior.
- Preserve compatibility only for truly external or persisted user data after an actual release, or when the user explicitly requests a migration path.
- Prefer clear, current architecture over supporting obsolete in-progress code.

```rust
// Bad: keep a legacy parser for an unreleased project format.
// Good: update the format and tests to the current intended structure.
```
